DTSTAMP:20260730T213746Z
DTSTART:20260804T123000Z
DTEND:20260804T143000Z
SUMMARY:Fascinating Light and Colour Phenomena in Nature
LOCATION:Conference Room II\, IIC main\, India International Centre\, 40 
 Max Mueller Marg\, Lodhi Gardens\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://iicdelhi.in/programmes/fascinating-light-and-colour-phenomena
 -nature
DESCRIPTION:As part of International Day of Light (IDL) Workshop 2026\nKe
 ynote Address: Photonics as a Key Enabling Technology: A Two-Way Link Bet
 ween Basic Research and Innovation by Prof. John M. Dudley\, Professor at
  the Université Marie et Louis Pasteur\, France\; International Day of L
 ight 2026 Steering Committee Chair\nWelcome Address: K.N. Shrivastava\, D
 irector\, IIC\nAddress: Dr. Tabassum Jamal\, IDL Workshop Chair\nOrganise
 d as part of the International Day of Light (IDL) 2026\, the workshop is 
 an introduction to the fascinating science of light and colour through ev
 eryday natural phenomena. Aligned with the UNESCO theme "Light for a Sust
 ainable Future\," it seeks to promote scientific awareness while highligh
 ting the role of light in sustainable development.\nThe inaugural session
  will be followed by a technical session featuring presentations by exper
 ts in the field\nFor more details\, please\nclick here\n(Collaboration: Z
 aheer Science Foundation\, New Delhi and Shanti Foundation International)
 \n\nhttps://iicdelhi.in/programmes/fascinating-light-and-colour-phenomena
 -nature
CATEGORIES:talk\,nature\,science
END:VEVENT
